ng, Yunnan, Zhejiang); Tibet; North Korea; South Korea; Bonin Isl. [I] (Chichijima [I]); Taiwan; Pakistan (Sind, Baluchistan, Waziristan, Kurram, Dir, Chitral, Swat, Hazara, Astor, Gilgit, Baltistan, Murree); Nepal; Bhutan; India (Gujarat, Jammu & Kashmir, Manipur, Punjab, Rajasthan, Madhya Pradesh, Tamil Nadu, Uttar Pradesh); Thailand; Laos; South China Sea Isl.; Lesser Sunda Isl. [I]; Easter Isl. [I]; USA [I] (California [I], Utah [I], Colorado [I], Arizona [I], New Mexico [I], Kansas [I], Oklahoma [I], Texas [I], Arkansas [I], Louisiana [I], Tennessee [I], Mississippi [I], Alabama [I], Florida [I]); Mexico [I]; Costa Rica [I]; Jamaica [I]; Hispaniola [I]; Virgin Isl. [I] (St. Croix [I]); Anguilla [I]; Antigua [I]; Aruba [I]; Bonaire [I]; Curacao [I]; Colombia [I]; Venezuela [I]; Bolivia [I]; Brazil [I]","","text","",""]]},"V4KMN":{"d":[["Distribution and ecology: — Habenaria brachycalcarata was found so far in the state of Goiás, Brazil (Figure 3), in the reservoir of the Schools of Agronomy, Veterinary Medicine and Animal Science of UFG, which is surrounded by riparian forests, seasonal forests and “ Veredas ”, in addition to being cultivated in the water tanks of the ETG between 713 and 788 m above sea level. It grows among floating and emerged aquatic macrophytes, such as Eichhornia crassipes Martius (1823: 9) Solms-Laubach (1883: 527) — Pontederiaceae Kunth (1815: 265), Azolla spp. and Salvinia spp. — Salviniaceae Martinov (1820: 559), and Pistia stratiotes Linnaeus (1753: 963) — Araceae Jussieu (1789: 23). The new species was observed flowering and fruiting between August and March. Because it presents small, inconspicuous, greenish flowers, and a very shortened spur, it is suggested that this species may be self-compatible and pollinated by crepuscular / nocturnal pollinators, such as small Lepidoptera and / or Diptera, possibly with a proboscis of similar length to the spur containing nectar inside, similarly to what is reported for other species of the genus (vide Singer & Cocucci 1997, Singer 2001, Singer et al. 2007, and Pedron et al. 2012).","","text","",""]]},"V4VVZ":{"d":[["Japan","2121","mrgid","",""]]},"V4W5Z":{"d":[["Maharashtra","48202","mrgid","",""]]},"V5LHQ":{"d":[["SE-Brazil (Minas Gerais, Espírito Santo, Rio de Janeiro)","","text","",""]]},"VC2S2":{"d":[["Venezuela","2201","mrgid","",""]]},"VC6JW":{"d":[["Missouri","48300","mrgid","",""]]},"W3T2":{"d":[["Gabon; Congo [Brazzaville]; Cabinda; D.R.Congo [Zaire]; Rwanda; Burundi; Uganda; Angola","","text","",""]]},"W42S":{"d":[["Madagascar","","text","",""]]},"W432":{"d":[["Vietnam","","text","",""]]},"WC4B":{"d":[["DR Congo, Malawi, Mozambique, South Africa","","text","",""]]},"YP3T":{"d":[["Pakistan (Chitral, Hindukush, Pamirs); NW-India (Himachal Pradesh, Jammu & Kashmir, Zanskar, Ladakh)","","text","",""]]},"YP43":{"d":[["China (Sichuan/Hubei border)","","text","",""]]},"YSLX":{"d":[["","MLY-SI","tdwg","native",""],["Singapore","","text","native",""]]},"YSM7":{"d":[["","MLY-SI","tdwg","native",""],["Malaysia (Penang), Singapore","","text","native",""]]},"ZLWS":{"d":[["Southern Asia","","text","",""]]},"ZM72":{"d":[["Europe & Northern Asia (excluding China)","","text","",""],["Southern Asia","","text","",""]]}}